meta {
  name: Pending Approvals
  type: http
  seq: 30
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/requests/pending-approvals
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

query {
  ~all: true
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    console.log("⏰", res.body.total, "ticket(s) awaiting approval in", res.body.groups.length, "role group(s)");
    res.body.groups.forEach(g => console.log("  •", g.label, "→", g.count, "| current:", g.isCurrentRole, "| switch:", g.canSwitch, "| ids:", g.ticketIds.join(",")));
  }
}

docs {
  # Pending Approvals (web + mobile)

  Tickets waiting for the **logged-in user's** approval, grouped by the **role + department**
  they must act as. Uses exactly the same rules as the pending-approval reminder push,
  so the total here matches the number in the notification
  ("⏰ Reminder: 15 tickets awaiting your approval").

  Works with **any** of the user's roles in the token — it looks at all roles the user holds,
  not only the current one.

  ## Query
  | Param | Default | Description |
  |-------|---------|-------------|
  | `all` | `false` | `false` = tickets pending **3+ days** (same as the notification). `true` = every pending ticket. |

  ## Who holds a ticket
  - **Stage 1 (`stage: "own"`)** — requestor's HOD has not approved → the requestor's HOD
    (the `hodEmpId` set on the requestor). Role to act as: `HOD` of the requestor's dept.
    - Requestor has no HOD set → not listed for anyone (fix the user in User Management).
    - Ticket raised to `Management` → not listed (HODs can't open those).
    - HOD is GN-01 / GN-02 → group `role: "Management"`, `openPath: "/management"`
      (they approve in the Management portal).
  - **Stage 2 (`stage: "assigned"`)** — HOD approved / forwarded, nobody in the assigned dept has acted
    → `RM`, `HOD`, `DeptHOD` of the assigned dept (own-dept tickets → `DeptHOD` only).
    Directly assigned to a person (`isDirectAssign`) → `DeptHOD` is not listed (they can't see it).
  - Only `Open` tickets. The requestor is never listed for their own ticket.
  - Calendar days. Stage 2 counts from the HOD approval / forward date.

  ## Response
  ```json
  {
    "total": 15,
    "minDays": 3,
    "currentRole": { "role": "HOD", "dept": "HR" },
    "groups": [
      {
        "role": "HOD",
        "dept": "HR",
        "label": "HOD — HR",
        "stage": "own",
        "isCurrentRole": true,
        "canSwitch": false,
        "accessible": true,
        "count": 14,
        "oldestDays": 131,
        "ticketIds": [101, 87, 64],
        "tickets": [
          {
            "id": 101,
            "empId": "GN-2001",
            "purpose": "New laptop",
            "requestorName": "Ravi Kumar",
            "dept": "HR",
            "assignedDept": "IT",
            "raisedAt": "2026-07-10T05:30:00.000Z",
            "pendingSince": "2026-07-10T05:30:00.000Z",
            "days": 131
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "role": "RM",
        "dept": "Facilities",
        "label": "Reporting Manager — Facilities",
        "stage": "assigned",
        "isCurrentRole": false,
        "canSwitch": true,
        "accessible": true,
        "count": 1,
        "oldestDays": 5,
        "ticketIds": [140],
        "tickets": [ ... ]
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  | Field | Meaning |
  |-------|---------|
  | `total` | Distinct tickets (a ticket held in two roles counts once) — matches the notification |
  | `groups[].role` / `dept` | The role + dept to act as — send these to **Switch Role** |
  | `isCurrentRole` | Already logged in as this role → no switch needed |
  | `canSwitch` | User holds this role in `user_roles` → can switch to it |
  | `accessible` | `isCurrentRole || canSwitch`. `false` → role not assigned to the user; show it disabled ("contact HR") |
  | `ticketIds` | Oldest first — use with `GET /requests?ids=...` |
  | `openPath` | Only on `role: "Management"` groups — open this portal instead of the dashboard list |
  | `tickets[].days` | Full days waiting in the current stage |

  Groups: current role first, then by count. Sum of group counts can be higher than `total`
  when the same ticket is waiting on the user in two roles.

  ## Client flow (web + mobile)
  1. Call this API → show one small card per group (count, role, dept, oldest days).
  2. User taps a group:
     - `isCurrentRole: false` → `POST /auth/switch-role` `{ "role": g.role, "dept": g.dept }`
       → save the new token.
  3. Load the tickets with the (new) token: `GET /requests?ids=<g.ticketIds joined by ,>`
     (one ticket → you can open `GET /requests/<id>` directly).

  Web does this in the **Pending Approvals** popup (cards), opened by the dashboard button
  and when the reminder notification is tapped (`/?pendingApprovals=1`).
}
